findings.body:
`IBookingRepository.updateMany` is declared as `Promise<{ count: number }>` (`packages/lib/server/repository/dto/IBookingRepository.ts:48`). The implementation in `BookingRepository.ts:1502` awaits `prismaClient.booking.updateMany` and returns nothing, so its return type is `Promise<void>`. Since `BookingRepository` declares `implements IBookingRepository`, `void` is not assignable to `{ count: number }`, and TypeScript reports an error on the class. The method also has broken indentation (`async` starts at column 0), which suggests it was pasted in without formatting.

::diff{file="packages/features/bookings/repositories/BookingRepository.ts" lines="1502-1507"}

The fix is to return the Prisma result, which is `{ count }`, so the implementation matches the interface. Callers in `handleCancelBooking.ts` do not use the return value, so returning it is harmless.
